<title>USA: BankAmerica to make &quot;major&quot; announcement.</title>
<headline>BankAmerica to make &quot;major&quot; announcement.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankAmerica Corp said on Tuesday that its chairman and chief executive, David Coulter, will make &quot;a major, positive announcement affecting 85,000 employees worldwide,&quot; at 1130 EST.</p>
<p>The company said the announcement will be made via live satellite broadcast from San Francisco to BankAmerica employees in 26 locations in the U.S. and overseas.</p>
<p>It said it will be the largest, most far-flung gathering of employees in the corporation's history, and that Coulter will answer questions afterward.</p>
</text>
